  "body": "Stacks on [REC PR #95](https://github.com/cosmosapjw-quantum/rec_bianchi/pull/95) at `a76cf0f3044f4946ee4a6c3eb1c9beec3405aee6`. **Draft scientific integration, no merge, no REI adoption.**\n\n**Implemented:** original HyRec October 2012 C `hydrogen.c::rec_HMLA_2photon_dxHIIdlna` compiled unmodified with a new thin persistent-history C wrapper; independent source-native H-only q0 accepted-history C and Python evolution, each maintaining its own xHII and 311 virtual + 3 Lyman columns. Zero-copy native `double **` arrays avoid quadratic full-history copying. First-order Euler xHII and positive implicit Compton + adiabatic Tm, synthetic zero photon prehistory starting z900; source DLNA exactly 8.49e-5.\n\n**Actual owner-PC execution before this publication:** 33 accepted points: maximum globally scaled relative photon/source discrepancy 4.2056406721019395e-13; 129 points: 6.076757312080765e-13. At 129, xe 1.84748e-14, Tm 5.55918e-16, ionization RHS 1.97929e-13, virtual 6.07676e-13, Lyman 2.82820e-13. Fresh full non-slow suite **488 PASS / 41 deselected**. Wolfram separately checked the temperature BE positivity/radiation cap and conditional Euler species bounds. Original physical source ZIP SHA256 `48cd597519606cdafd0ee6405b781d28467cd323278d16596055a8d0577a1d27`.\n\n**Strict limitations:** this comparison is two independently evolving but **synthetic, FLRW q0, H-only** test trajectories that share H(z), nH(z) and the thermal law. It is **not** a physically initialized full primordial H+He history, not the original source's higher-order history integrator, not a high-z signed Bianchi model and not a REI sensitivity run. No CMB observable or improved physical recombination error is claimed.\n\n**Infrastructure:** SSH to actual NCP `s1a0e5abed09` confirmed 64 CPUs, ~125GiB RAM and rustc/cargo 1.99.0. NCP default Python lacks NumPy/SciPy. Isolated environment installation was blocked; Desktop Commander monthly usage limit subsequently prevented further remote execution. **NCP scientific run NOT_RUN.** Source files were re-authored via GitHub connector after local host tool limit, and read back from this branch; full test command has **NOT** rerun on the published remote blob. Local worktree remains uncommitted; reconcile before pull. Native subagent not available.\n\nAll claims and next actions in `research/rec_r3e_full_history_20261015/EVIDENCE.json` and `REPORT_KO.md`. Dropbox+Google Drive double cloud backup for this R3e unit remains **not verified** due owner-device tool limit. Earlier R3d double backup is separate.\n\nNext high-value physics action: start from source-physical radiation prehistory and helium chemistry for independent full primordial solution; separately run recipient PR150 fresh native charge/energy/opacity sensitive initial-state cases after its transport gates.",
